<h2>No installer in your state yet?</h2>
<p>The network does not cover every state. If yours is open, do not settle for a trench by default. Use the <a href="/find-a-contractor">request a contractor</a> form, tell us where the property is and what the pipe is doing, and we will locate a qualified cured in place pipe contractor near you and have them get in touch. The <a href="/network-map">network map</a> shows which states are covered, which are partly covered and which are open.</p>

<h2>Emergency? Read this first</h2>
<p>If sewage is backing up into the house right now, the first call is to a drain cleaning company or your plumber to get the line flowing, and if the problem is at the city main, to your utility. Lining is not an emergency service; it is the permanent fix you schedule once the pipe is open and you have the camera recording in hand. Keep that recording. It is exactly what a lining contractor needs to quote from.</p>
